  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_38dd984daccf45b9b42446121f793ef7",
      "statement": "A security valuation is a per-user fair-value range: `SecurityValuationModel` maps to `market_security_valuations` with `user_id` (a plain UUID, no FK to `auth_users`), a cascading `security_id` FK to `market_securities.id`, non-null `lower_bound`/`upper_bound` declared as `DECIMAL(16,8)`, and created/updated timestamps, with `UniqueConstraint(\"user_id\", \"security_id\", name=\"valuation_user_security_unique\")` plus the index `ix_market_security_valuations_user_security` over the same pair -- so there is at most one range per (user, security).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/market/model.py#L241-L267",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e5e6030ee352985c0fca02a28f99d326f23bb13440b2ca0059a5c99e676adb02:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e7882e1fde574180b8856b85c2913cc2",
      "statement": "`migrations/versions/3436586a755f_create_security_valuations.py` (down_revision `4c2ed77e7738`) is the Alembic revision that creates `market_security_valuations` with its cascading foreign key, primary key, the `valuation_user_security_unique` unique constraint and the non-unique `ix_market_security_valuations_user_security` index, and its `downgrade()` drops the index and table, demonstrating the repository rule that a model change ships its revision in the same change under the `<hash>_<description>.py` naming convention.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://migrations/versions/3436586a755f_create_security_valuations.py#L15-L47",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5c0db5d265dd175d621e03bc10f7c94c71f06006628de63dddc886a26927fb74:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_db271849850a480fb76be0dd765075df",
      "statement": "`SecurityValuationRepository` in `src/market/repository.py` is a router-only ABC with exactly three methods -- `get_by_security_and_user`, `upsert`, `get_batch_by_user_and_securities` -- and its SQLAlchemy implementation filters every statement by `user_id`, so no read or write can cross users.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/market/repository.py#L316-L336",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0dff9df1d2982d353e8b70441589312fc848994fbc75a1c946df85224570d9ff:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/market/repository_sqlalchemy.py#L1298-L1355",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8832ce0f091bd47266634c5542644bcc72919f8c44d3bbe8d401d49a6a9aabff:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_04b1de9b9e5e4536959b9f17f39bfed4",
      "statement": "`SqlAlchemySecurityValuationRepository.upsert` selects the `(security_id, user_id)` row and either overwrites `lower_bound`/`upper_bound` with `updated_at = datetime.now(UTC)` or inserts a new row with both timestamps, then commits and refreshes -- making the write idempotent (a second upsert returns the same row `id`, as the repository test asserts) without relying on the model's `onupdate`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/market/repository_sqlalchemy.py#L1312-L1342",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b080413b9e4f34dc250b07b54b4340ead7addeaf17c12d5d57756ab555e4a2f4:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/market/test_security_valuation_repository.py#L92-L116",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:406be70da5a08e5dcf35ff08e526e0586ccf7384b04aebd0f6fa9a249af744e4:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b0019280372348bf8490d175f2ab9a61",
      "statement": "`get_batch_by_user_and_securities` returns `[]` immediately for an empty id list and otherwise issues one `IN` query scoped by `user_id`, so batch reads return only the subset of requested securities that the caller actually has a range for (a second user's row for the same security is excluded, as the repository test asserts).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/market/repository_sqlalchemy.py#L1344-L1355",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8db96baced86c25378259014fc61b42952fc25031025b107888acb52653bacaa:"
        },
        {
