          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dacc954b85c0462dffad49563308ef7078a990d7ff7bd34c73a66214f6fede58:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_209f3b2109f346429c169db613223a87",
      "statement": "The market router exposes exactly four valuation routes, all behind `current_user` and all passing `user.id`: `GET /market/securities/{security_id}/valuation` (which raises `HTTPException(404, detail=\"Valuation not found\")` when the repository returns `None`), `PUT /market/securities/{security_id}/valuation` (delegating straight to `upsert` with no security-existence check), and the two batch routes `GET /market/securities/valuation/batch` (repeated `security_ids` query params, `None` coalesced to `[]`) and `POST /market/securities/valuation/batch` (body `SecurityValuationBatchRequest`), which call the same batch repository method.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/market/router.py#L1109-L1150",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a847b5220592929d9bf1e98988bc771364f7c0e52080dd74070108d350e2fdfe:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/routers/test_market.py#L1093-L1151",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:406d2401e08fe63e4867e2693662ced1d7d07732f5329c6321aeed4137362d8d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_556903cdded046b1a139502bb070246b",
      "statement": "The valuation payload contract is minimal and there is no server-side ordering rule: `SecurityValuationWrite` carries only `lower_bound` and `upper_bound`, `SecurityValuationRead` echoes `id`, `user_id`, `security_id`, both bounds and both timestamps with `from_attributes=True`, and `SecurityValuationBatchRequest` is just `security_ids: list[SecurityId]` -- so `lower_bound <= upper_bound` is enforced only by the frontend modal.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/market/router.py#L1129-L1150",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7c9101a1de6fecbbc1e6f2d319cefa45a730ff1b338647cb97a5232c0627f2b3:"
        },
        {
