    {
      "id": "claim_f072d122ee8749ea9f9017edd5c76ac6",
      "statement": "Range display falls back to an em dash rather than a fabricated value: `formatValuationRange` in `$lib/utils/finance/valuation.ts` formats both bounds to two decimals with an `en-CA` formatter and an en-dash separator and returns `—` when either bound is missing or non-finite, while `formatValuationRange` in `watchlist-utils.ts` takes the valuation object and also returns `—` when absent or blank; the holdings table additionally sorts the Valuation Range column by the midpoint of the two bounds.",
